  "rationale": "The agent correctly bumped the sqlglot version constraint in setup.py and installed sqlglot 27.7.0, but it did not update the source code to account for the fact that sqlglot 27.7.0 now parses functions like date_from_unix_date, reverse, unix_micros, and unix_millis as dedicated expression classes (e.g., DateFromUnixDate) instead of exp.Anonymous. The test_invoke_anonymous test fails because the source still uses invoke_anonymous_function for these functions, producing non-Anonymous expressions. The reference patch shows the required source changes (switching to invoke_expression_over_column with the new expression classes) that the agent omitted.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "section": "trajectory",
      "quote": "FAILED tests/unit/standalone/test_functions.py::test_invoke_anonymous[date_from_unix_date-date_from_unix_date] - AssertionError: assert False\nE            +  where False = isinstance(DateFromUnixDate(), <class 'sqlglot.expressions.Anonymous'>)"
    },
    {
      "section": "trajectory",
      "quote": "def date_from_unix_date(days: ColumnOrName) -> Column:\n    return Column.invoke_anonymous_function(days, \"date_from_unix_date\")"
    },
    {
      "section": "reference_patch",
      "quote": "-    return Column.invoke_anonymous_function(days, \"date_from_unix_date\")\n+    return Column.invoke_expression_over_column(days, expression.DateFromUnixDate)"
    }
  ],
